          "emptyHint": "JSON oben einfügen oder Beispiel testen. Ein Array aus Objekten konvertiert am besten: jedes Objekt wird eine Zeile. Ein einzelnes Objekt wird eine Zeile.",
          "parseErrorTitle": "Das ist noch kein gültiges JSON.",
          "parseErrorText": "The browser parser stopped here:",
          "parseErrorHint": "Common causes: a missing comma or quote, a trailing comma after the last item, single quotes instead of double quotes, or comments — JSON allows none of those. This tool never guesses a repair, because a guessed comma can change your data.",
          "errorEmptyArray": "The JSON is an empty array, so there are no rows and no columns to export. Add at least one object, for example [{\"id\":1}].",
          "errorMixedArray": "This array mixes objects with plain values or nested arrays, so it cannot become a clean table. Make every item an object — or, for a simple list, remove the objects so each value lands in one 'value' column.",
          "errorNoColumns": "These objects have no fields, so there are no columns to export. CSV needs at least one named field per row.",
          "errorShape": "CSV needs rows, and a single number, text value or true/false cannot become a table. Wrap your records in an array of objects — [{\"id\":1},{\"id\":2}] — or paste one object to convert it as a single row.",
